              "login": "EagleClaw89"
            },
            "body": "Data point for this docs change, from 2x DGX Spark (GB10).\n\nModel: `Qwen4ExpForConditionalGeneration` (`model_type qwen4_exp`, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next NVFP4). Top-level config has no `max_position_embeddings` or `rope_parameters`; both live under `text_config` (`text_config.rope_parameters.rope_type = default`).\n\nWe passed a flat override:\n\n```\n--hf-overrides '{\"max_position_embeddings\":1048576,\"rope_parameters\":{\"rope_type\":\"yarn\",\"factor\":4.0, ...}}' --max-model-len 1048576\n```\n\nvLLM accepted the override, applied it to the wrong object, kept the derived length at 262144 and then rejected the length:\n\n```\nValidationError: 1 validation error for ModelConfig\n  Value error, User-specified max_model_len (1048576) is greater than the derived max_model_len\n  (max_position_embeddings=262144.0 or model_max_length=None in model's config.json) ...\n```\n\nNesting under `text_config` fixed it. The error text points at `VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN`, not at the override shape, so we spent a boot cycle on it (three engines died in about 30 s each). Suggestions: (1) this doc note, (2) a warning when a top-level override key exists only under `text_config` of a composite config.\n\nCaveat: if `--max-model-len` had not been set above the native length (for example a rope-only override), we expect the override would be dropped with no error at all; we did not test that case.\n\n_Drafted with AI assistance (Claude); reviewed and approved by the author._\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-16T18:57:15Z",
            "databaseId": 6222591036,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-16T18:57:15Z",
